# ACT ONE

INT. COFFEE SHOP - DAY

A small neighborhood coffee shop. Morning light streams through large windows.

ALEX (30s, sharp eyes) stares at a laptop screen. An empty espresso cup sits nearby.

ALEX
(muttering)
Come on, load already.

The screen flickers. Alex leans forward.

ALEX (CONT'D)
There it is.

Alex types rapidly.

EXT. CITY STREET - DAY

Alex bursts through the door, laptop bag over one shoulder. The city hums with
midday traffic.

ALEX
(into phone)
I found it. Meet me at the park in ten.

Alex disappears into the crowd.

INT. PARK PAVILION - DAY

A covered pavilion beside a small lake. A FEW PIGEONS pick at crumbs.

MORGAN (40s, cautious) waits at a picnic table. Alex arrives, breathless.

MORGAN
You said it was urgent.

ALEX
It is.

Alex opens the laptop, turns the screen to face Morgan.

MORGAN
(reading)
This can't be right.

ALEX
But it is. And we have forty-eight hours.

Morgan stands, paces.

MORGAN
Alright. What do we need?

ALEX
Three things. Access, time, and a very good alibi.

EXT. ROOFTOP - NIGHT

City lights spread below. Alex and Morgan stand at the railing.

MORGAN
After tonight nothing is the same.

ALEX
It never was.

They both look out at the city.

FADE OUT.

THE END
